00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:20.800
<v Orlando>This is <lang pt-BR>Tá Falado</lang> and this is lesson number
five on the disappearing reflexive verbs.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:25.800
<v Orlando>As always, I'm Orlando Kelm, that doesn't change,
and I'm here with Valdo, Michelle and José Luis,

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:26.730
<v Michelle>And that doesn't change.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.990
<v José Luis>Hi there.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.040
<v Orlando>Disappearing reflexive verbs: why are
we calling that the name of our lesson?

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:43.062
<v Michelle>Yeah, there are a lot of reflexive verbs in Spanish, and they
use reflexive verbs, but in Portuguese sometimes we use it,

00:00:43.062 --> 00:00:45.550
<v Michelle>sometimes not, it's not a rule.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:52.250
<v Orlando>Exactly. So as we hear our dialogue today, you're going to
hear a number of verbs where in Spanish they're reflexive.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:54.050
<v Orlando><lang pt-BR>Levantar</lang>, right?

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.300
<v José Luis><lang es>Se levantó.</lang>

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:59.800
<v Orlando>But in Portuguese, when you say those verbs, you just say…

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:00.800
<v Valdo><lang pt-BR>Levantou.</lang>

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:01.800
<v Orlando>Exactly.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.800
<v Valdo>You don't use it reflexively.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:08.800
<v Valdo>Yeah, actually the grammar books say we have to use them,
but in everyday conversation people don't actually use them.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:09.800
<v Orlando>That's a good point.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:10.800
<v Michelle>In conversation people don't use them.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:11.090
<v Valdo>The grammar book says you should.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.800
<v Michelle>The tendency is not to use them.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:14.800
<v Valdo>Yeah, all right.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:15.090
<v Michelle>Most people don't.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:20.600
<v Orlando>So, we're going to be talking about the use of coupons,
which Michelle finds a fantastic thing about this country.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:25.729
<v Orlando>And as we're talking about coupons, listen to verbs
that should be reflexive in your Spanish brain,

00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:28.500
<v Orlando>but are not reflexive when you say them in Portuguese.

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:31.140
