<v Valdo><lang pt-BR>Senta</lang>, <lang pt-BR>senta</lang>, <lang pt-BR>sente-se</lang>, <lang pt-BR>senta</lang>.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:28.850
<v Michelle>Yeah, we mix it up.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:29.800
<v Valdo>Yeah, we mix, uh-huh.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.750
<v Valdo>Either way, reflexive or not.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.000
<v Orlando>And I was actually thinking you can
kind of do that in English, right?

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.300
<v Orlando>You can say "sit down", "sit yourself down".

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:44.000
<v Orlando>You could say it that way too. That's kind of what's
happening here. Brazilians are using it and not using it.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.850
<v Orlando>We also saw the verb <lang pt-BR>lembrar</lang>, which means to remember.

